r","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-23T07:47:35-08:00","id":1169916,"title":"","content":"Looks like the blessings narrowly have it! Time to get started then <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-23T13:06:12-08:00","id":1169987,"title":"","content":"Right, these are gonna trickle in over the next coupla days rather than getting delivered in one hefty chunk - getting used to a new laptop, and my wrists are aching a bit as they adapt to the slightly different spacing and layout on the keys. Anyways, it's also Christmas Eve tomorrow and I'm currently visiting the in-laws - and here in Poland, they do all the Xmas celebrations on the Eve rather than the Day, meaning I'll likely have only limited time to type tomorrow!<br /> <br /> \u200bWithout further ado, though, I'll begin!<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">\u200bEleven Shaman Blessings - A Bag Of Tricks And Secrets</span><br /> Most shamans have one - a bag of tricks, a bundle of old secrets, a handful of knick-knacks, the grisly contents of a gris-gris bag. Some have more than one; some are bedecked with the things, a veritable occult Christmas tree. Look inside, peer into the gloom; trinkets and curios, reminders of old bargains and metaphysical shortcuts, emergency supplies for the sacrifice and the offering. A fragment of an ancient crown, a tattered scrap of skin inked with a forgotten name, a vial of engine oil, a piece of bone with the faces of enemies etched into it. It's a Swiss army knife of solutions to problems, the anchor for a memory palace of old lore that a life might depend on in the heat of the moment.<br /> <br /> \u200bReach in, take hold of one of the tricks or trinkets, and draw it out. What do we have first? A knot of gold and bone; a king's ransom, and a king's sacrifice.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Lo, The King Of Frost And Shadow</span></b><br /> The immense power of the turning seasons is hardly a secret to spiritual intercessors and shamans. Many ritemasters know the simple lore required to tap into the Essence generated through the metaphysical turbine of the world's turning nature, and the sheer impact of such profound seasonal changes can be witnessed in how it sculpts both Flesh and Shadow alike.<br /> <br /> Away from the equatorial regions, where the seasons shift to the greatest extremes, there comes a point in the long dark of winter where light and life seem perilously far away. The gloom and the cold of the Flesh are matched by the tyranny of the writhing, capering spirits of darkness and ice in the Spirit. Strength wanes, resources dwindle, hope dies. There's a reason humans often throw celebrations and feasts in midwinter - a spark of heat, a spark of joy, a reminder that the darkness will come to and end. For the Uratha, there's more to it than just that. Look into the frozen gloom, imagine the compass-point of that great, turning wheel of seasons approaching, the apex of mid-winter when the grim Essence of the season is at its peak - and is about to begin its retreat. Seize hold of the spoke as it passes; seize hold of the power it offers. Bless the land and the people. Kindle a flame from a spark. Better one dies so that many may live.<br /> <br /> You're going to need a sacrifice.<br /> <br /> They must be human, but they don't need to be willing. There are some ceremonial forms you will have to adhere to, though. This needs to be done right to work. No skimping, no skipping steps. Blood on the snow isn't enough. It needs to be blood fed, made fat with rewarded hopes and sated hungers, and not just a spattering libation but a river upon which the darkness can let itself be carried. If you're going to tap the well of winter's frigid power, you have to provide a fine vehicle for the season's journey.<br /> <br /> Take one healthy human (they need to have all their health levels intact, at least prior to the bit where their life functionally ends). Treat them to a feast. For one cycle of the sun and moon, treat them as a king or queen, a monarch of mid-winter. Ply them with fine foods and fine goods - don't skimp, or this will not work, and all you'll have is a dead body and a lot of wasted time. You need to offer them the best you have. Bedeck them in grand clothes, refill their cup, laugh and dance with them. Indulge their passions. You need to indulge their Virtue and their Vice before midnight passes; you need to fulfil who and what they are, so that they feel centred and assured of their being. You're werewolves; this shouldn't be too hard.<br /> <br /> Here's an important part: find out a desire of theirs that is not about their immediate indulgence. Find out something that they want, in the long term - maybe for prosperity for their people, maybe for the defeat of an enemy, maybe for their name to be remembered. You need that desire, whether self-centred or altruistic, and it needs to be a real desire of theirs. Still, cull the offered desires carefully: cast aside anything impossible or nonsensical, or anything that would do you harm or trouble (unless you're feeling particularly guilty about all this and feel you need to be punished in some sort of self-martyrdom complex). After all, fulfilling the desire is something that you're going to be setting a large number of spirits to the task of. Again, obviously, a desire that rests on the necessity of the mid-winter king's continued life is not going to work out. You may need to pull a few conversational tricks to pull an appropriate desire out of the sacrifice's mind.<br /> <br /> If the day's monarch knows what's coming, you might want to sugar the experience with offering them the ceremonial right to make a few other orders, decisions and choices that will last beyond their death. Up to you though, really. If mid-winter decides it wants to play with their vessel for a little while they might retain some semblance of who they were, after all, and they might be a bit miffed if they've made a deal with you that you decide not to carry through. A lot of shamans prefer to butter the sacrifice up with good behaviour, just in case.<br /> <br /> You've prepared your mid-winter king. Now the second part - the rites. Firstly, you're going to need to declare a Sacred Hunt against the king. That's simple enough, but there's an extra restriction you need to obey to get the second rite you're going to perform to stick - the hunt needs to either be a genuine pursuit through cold and dark, or it needs to be a willing sacrifice. So, you can either give your gold-clad, well-fed king a chance to run - maybe an hour or so of a head start in the gloom of night? Maybe give them a ceremonial weapon, just to make it feel like they have a chance? - or you make sure they walk to the altar of their own volition, knowing that they are about to be offered up so that the people may survive winter. Just gut the poor bugger on the spot, without even asking for permission, and you'll have completed your Sacred Hunt but the final rite isn't going to work.<br /> <br /> There is a way round this, though most Uratha won't encounter it. Rather than a Sacred Hunt performed by werewolves, an entirely human pack (or one with Wolf-Blooded or Claimed) can go through the same motions - a ritualised hunt or willing sacrifice) and prime the second rite just as effectively. Why's that? Best ask the hoary old elders of the glaciers and the places where darkness has never been broken by light; they're the only ones likely to remember.<br /> <br /> Got your sacrifice ready, then? Voluntary, or you've chased them through the snow and the Rahu has their throat in his jaws after a good run that's really got the blood pumping?<br /> <br /> Now the second rite, then. Bless the land. Bless the people. Bless the darkness and the earth, the frost and the fire.<br /> <br /> Storm Lords do their best to forge agreements with the nobles of darkness and ice so that none will take the open vessel of the sacrifice. Such spirits tend to levy a painful price in some other way.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">King Of Frost And Shadow (Pack Rite \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</span></b><br /> This rite is an offering to the spirits of the changing seasons. It harnesses the power of darkness, death and cold that peaks at mid-winter, and balances the scales with the spirits that now begin to wax in power.<br /> <br /> <b>Symbols:</b> Blood, gold, food, winter.<br /> <br /> <b>Action: </b>Extended (5 successes; each roll represents a single turn)<br /> <br /> <b>Success:</b> The rite can only be performed the night of mid-winter; it requires a single human who must have been plied with the finest food and gifts the pack can offer, who must have had both their Vice and Virtue fulfilled within the past day, and who the ritemaster must know a single desire of. The sacrifice must be willing, or to have been successfully subjected to a Siskur-Dah involving a meaningful pursuit and hunt; alternatively, a pack that does not include Uratha can go through the same motions without requiring a proper Sacred Hunt rite performance.<br /> <br /> Upon success, the human must be lethally wounded by the ritemaster, who speaks the sacrifice's desire; the sacrifice is immediately Open to any powerful spirit of darkness, winter or cold of Rank 3 or more that chooses to Claim them. Such a spirit may immediately Claim them, without need of any period of Urging beforehand; the human victim is not able to mount any sort of resistance, even if they are possessed of any supernatural capabilities themselves. If no spirit is present and willing to Claim them, the sacrifice dies; either torn apart by the pack or, if the pack does not act to do so, they will literally rot and collapse in a flash of fast-forward decay, maggots churning them rapidly into dirt.<br /> <br /> Once the sacrifice is done, several effects begin across the pack's territory, and will hold until the season passes; if a spirit has Claimed the sacrifice, the effect will also end early if the Claimed is slain or driven away. Pack members gain a +3 bonus to all dice pools to resist privations from cold, hunger, disease and fatigue, and reduce damage from cold sources by 3; humans in the territory gain a +2 bonus and reduce the damage by 2; animals across the territory gain a +1 bonus and reduce the damage by 1. All loci across the territory produce 2 additional Essence each day, regardless of their dot rating. Inhabitants of the territory will find their Resources dot rating increased by 1 for a random period of time at some stage during the season; there is no way to predict when or how this windfall will occur. Spirits of ice and darkness gain a +1 bonus to their Power attribute, but do not gain a more favourable attitude to the pack; if anything, some will be riled and angered at the audacity of the pack in trying to seize the power of the wheel of seasons, and binding them to a task. If a pack member (human, Wolf-Blooded or werewolf) sacrifices another human being outside during a winter's night, they gain Influence (Cold) or Influence (Darkness); once the total dot rating of the uses they have made of it is equal to the health levels that the sacrificed human being had, they lose the ability.<br /> <br /> Finally, the local spirits of cold and dark will set about trying to make the sacrifice's desire come to pass. If an enemy was named, they will do their best to bring the victim down; they will steal into the Flesh to try and manipulate or curse or guide human pawns to see a plan through; and they will use the full array of their numina and capabilities in the process. What they will not and cannot do is approach the pack for aid or attempt to involve the pack in any way; and oft, the spirits will seek to cause the pack harm or trouble in how the desire plays out. By the time the season ends, if the spirits have not been successful, then they will be released from this ban - but it will not be possible to name and sacrifice a new king of frost and shadow in the region until another ten years have passed.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-23T13:44:59-08:00","id":1169998,"title":"","content":"Wow. That's perfect. And totally something I can use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-23T13:58:54-08:00","id":1170002,"title":"","content":"Well, that's some really cool &quot;trick&quot;. It also gives me an idea for a story hook about such Sacred Hunt going wrong- that is, the pack believes that it has made sure there is no high Ranked spirit which is willing and able to Claim the sacrifice is around, but they aren't aware of the fact that there is some sleeping horror beneath the surface, and the tickling of blood has awakened it from its sleep. Suddenly, the Claimed king rise from the dead- and the long winter can finally begin.<br /> <br /> Also, I'm so going to add reference to this in my Awful Ice project","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":503,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","user":"LostLight","date":". 12-23-2017, 05:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-23T14:11:40-08:00","id":1170005,"title":"","content":"Let the cold and dark of winter fade, put the gold and bone back in. Swirl the bag and its crude contents, its trinkets and charms and dried threads of sinew, reach once more and pluck out... a thumb drive?<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>We Shall Salt The Hard Drives Of Your Enemies</b></span><br /> There's a ping - new email has just landed in your inbox. You thumb the screen; there it is, an interesting title, might have something to do with the thing you're working on. Open. Ah, but it's a disappointment, just a clever spam trick. Headlined with something generic: CONGRATULATIONS! YOU ARE BLESSED! Probably a chain letter, right? It'll have something at the end like 'Please donate to the holy church of who gives a fuck' or 'send this email on to five more people within the day or you will be cursed!' or whatever hogwash. So you close it, maybe delete it. On with your day.<br /> <br /> You don't read the bits further down. SPIRITS OF WELL-BEING WILL WATCH OVER YOU. Not like you'd pay it any heed anyway, right? Who believes in spirits and guardian angels? YOUR ENEMIES WILL BE PLAGUED BY A SWARM OF VEXING FLIES. Even if you saw that, even if you remembered it and it maybe, possibly, tickled your amusement at the thought of that idiot in the office, it's not like it ever ends up happening; you never see them being pursued by angry wasps or whatever. MISFORTUNE WILL BEFALL THOSE WHO PLAN EVIL AGAINST YOU AND THEIR PLANS WILL WITHER. Yeah, but, seriously, it's not like you have enemies, not really.<br /> <br /> And off you go about your day.<br /> <br /> That dickhead in the office, though, see, he really doesn't like you. He sends a few nasty emails to the manager, complaining about how you're in late for work or you're behind on something or whatever petty shit it is that he's trying to leverage against you. He hits send and sits back, smug and satisfied about his incredibly inane scheme to undermine you and get the promotion instead of you. Then his phone pings. An email! Looks like it's from his wife so of course he opens it and... what? Fuck, spam. No, worse. A virus? What the shit? Aren't mail clients supposed to protect against that? He swears, but it's nothing too bad; just some stupid pop-up an- what? Shit, the inbox is filling up fast. Not viruses now, but... someone's signed him up to the internet's ten busiest porn sites catering to the most perverted and deviant tastes? He tries to send an angry email to tech support; it seems to work, but he doesn't get the message that the sending's actually failed until ten days later. When he gets home, hard-selling phone salesmen ring five or six times that evening, and one manages to call at three in the morning. He climbs into the car in the morning, and the radio breaks; it gets stuck on the channel with that genre of music he really hates. He gets in and the computer's extra slow to start-up. He fires up the email client, and it's full of porn. Again. He catches the manager, at least; a brief smile as he asks what she thinks of the things he complained about. She looks at him blankly; she hasn't received any emails from him.<br /> <br /> At that moment, a porn pop-up appears on his screen and starts playing a video. Loudly.<br /> <br /> A true shaman has a wide range of occult tools available. Some are potent workings, mighty rites and complex spirit bargains. This is not one of those; this is a petty little fucker that sits right at the bottom of the hierarchy, just under 'physically eat the dog that keeps waking you at night with its barking' but slightly above 'bind a disease spirit to curse someone with boils'. It's a blessing and a curse packaged together in a nifty little data package carefully wrapped by one of the more insalubrious data spirits sluicing around in the gutter of the infostream. Fairly cheap to bargain for - it's not going to cost you an arm or a leg - and in return you get one email packed with spiritual juice. All you need to do is send it, a one-shot digital berserker with very, very low horizons.<br /> <br /> There's a catch: the person you send it to, the recipient of the blessing, can't know it's from you. They also can't be an Uratha, only a Wolf-Blooded or mundane human being. Finally, you cannot intend to harm a specific target with the email's ensuing curses; this has to be done as a blessing for the recipient, not as an attempt to weaponise it against your own enemies, or else the data spirits just <i>cannot </i>make the deal with you in the first place. They are literally incapable of doing so; your intent is like a key to the metaphysical lock here.<br /> <br /> As soon as the recipient opens it, the blessing kicks in. They won't notice anything particularly beneficial happening to them. They probably won't notice the unpleasantness that happens to people who act against them either. But for a month, anyone who tries to harm them, undermine them, or otherwise wrong them - as per whether it would, by the opinion of the shaman, be something that would be a wrong - gets absolutely buggered by the worst symptoms of the modern data age's sicker corners. They get deluged with spam. If there's a slight chink in their digital armour, they'll get hacked. Got a wallet of bitcoin? Bad luck, your hard drive just corrupted and it's gone; you accidentally deleted the backups. Adblockers stop working. SMS messages get lost in the system. Your phone number appears on the call lists for the worst boiler-room scams in the region. Random, petty shit plagues you when it comes to technology. In Biblical times the shaman would have cursed you with a plague of locusts; in this era, the bugs are all virtual.<br /> <br /> The plague won't be lethal; nothing will go so catastrophically wrong that it threatens the victims' lives, although some might be driven to drastic or stupid actions as a result of it all. If the shaman tells the recipient that they sent the email, the whole thing ends; if the recipient feels sympathy for one of the victims of all the awful, the effect ends on that victim (unless they start scheming or undermining the blessed one again). If lots of people are cursed at the same time, the effects across all of them will be lessened; the spiritual workings of the spamurai email can't handle more than half a dozen victims, after which it degrades fast. One month after the email is sent, it all ends anyway.<br /> <br /> Werewolves are immune to the effects of the spam curse, as are spirits. Other supernatural beings, curiously enough, are not; if anything, they're affected worse. The limits that the blessed email can't cause lethal or life-threatening problems for them are removed, and spam curses unleashed in this way have an alarming tendency to mutate, become self-aware, and then try and murder their victims in as grotesque a fashion as possible. There's nothing quite like seeing a changeling holding up an iphone that's literally screaming in rage at them and trying to broadcast a frequency declaring an all-you-can-eat-buffet to any dangerous fae entities in the area, or an abyssal virus hijacking a mage's earbuds to dump raw Paradox into their skull.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":14}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-23T14:23:50-08:00","id":1170011,"title":"","content":"I LOVE IT SANTA CLAWS! <br /> <br /> Seriously, that curse is all kinds of awesome. I love it when urban fantasy plays with modern technology for all it's worth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-23T14:32:53-08:00","id":1170016,"title":"","content":"I smiled at that digital plague. <br /> <br /> Seriously, anyone who keeps saying that tech doesn\u2019t mix with magic/spirits/gods/the supernatural is a damn liar!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-23T14:45:38-08:00","id":1170020,"title":"","content":"Put the thumb drive carefully aside. Ignore the angry buzzing coming from within it. Tip something else out of the bag - a carefully folded piece of paper. This one's a list of names, each of them with a brief scribble of how grave or grand the favour owed by them is. This isn't just a booklet of bribes due or protection money owed, though - the people on this list are indebted to the shaman for more than just earthly gifts.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The Petitioner And The Wolf: A Tale Of Passions And Poor Choices</span></b><br /> Not every blessing of the Shadow is meant for the claws of the Uratha. A shaman is still needed as intercessor, of course - as go-between for Flesh and Spirit, as the bargainer who pays the price to the courts and choirs and broods - but the result is a gift, not a Gift; a brief bestowment of the Shadow's strength to a vessel purely of Flesh, one within whom the river of Essence can briefly, furiously course before washing out and being done. Not every spirit can give this blessing, and plenty that can just won't; it takes a little piece of them away, threads it through the shaman and into the final recipient. Until the blessing expires, the shaman gains the Ban condition in accordance with that of the spirit, and is unable to regain Essence from a locus or Sacred Hunt.<br /> <br /> \u200b(There are mortal occultists who manage to circumvent the need for the Uratha entirely, who manage to dabble with the Shadow and entreat the spirits directly. Theirs is a very, very dangerous path and this is not the place for their story).<br /> <br /> How does the shaman pay the price to the spirits? Oh, that depends, that varies, that is up to so many different factors and vagaries that there's no easy way to offer a list of what a shaman might pay. Some spirits care but a little, others are miserly or opportunistic and charge a ransom for even the slightest ember of their power. The key thing is, though, that the werewolf is serving as a middleman in this transaction, gleaning not a talen as the outcome but something stranger and decidedly costlier - a bundle of promised power that isn't quite physical at all, but that they can taste on their breath for as long as they bear it, that they can scent at the edge of their awareness. It's a hot potato; its presence fuzzes and stings, and it cools fast. Get it to the recipient quick.<br /> <br /> It's for a human being, see. It's a brief, surging pyre of Essence woven as the Influence of the spirits who have given it. It's a short ticket to a show of power - One Night Only, See The Amazing Avenger Wield The Power Of Fire! Come One, Come All, Witness The Incredible Speed Of The Desperate Competitor! Better than paying a hitman or doping or trying to be your own private detective or relying on your own clumsy, awkward words; a hit of Influence, anywhere from one to the full five dots, yours to command for the span of a day. It can't take root in just anybody, though; there's a reason human occultists who do manage to harness the power of the spirits use the strange and alien rites and practices they do. This? This isn't safe; it's mainlining spiritual cocaine. The recipient needs to be ready to take it, and that means they need to be obsessed with something, fuelled by passion and intense emotion.<br /> <br /> The human must be angry, bitter, hateful, euphoric, desperate, something that gives the blessing purchase in the drip-drip of Resonance that they're bleeding off. It needs something that's a major Aspiration for them, something that aligns with either their Virtue or their Vice, and that has meaning to them and their desires above all else. The cheated spouse who wants vengeance? The would-be hero who thinks he can make a difference to what's going on tonight and is willing to put his life on the line? The virtuoso going up against the greatest challenge of her career, who is absolutely terrified of failure and eager for anything that might give her an edge? They'll do. The pack's human footsoldier dully submitting to a shaman's attempt to weaponise him? Nah. There's nothing there for the madness of what's being performed to really latch onto.<br /> <br /> The blessing is bestowed in a way representing the Influence; the shaman sears a brand into the human for Fire, or demands a perverted indulgence for Lust, or something else. When the deal's sealed, the shaman feels something in her tugging at her own spirit - she's still the middleman here, serving as a channel between spirit and human. The human can use the Influence much like a werewolf with a talen, but the Influence is accessible for the full day's duration of the blessing; the human does not gain an actual Essence pool, but can use Influences of Essence cost totalling the shaman's Resolve + Composure per hour, no restriction on how many dots on the maximum level other than it's capped at 5 (ie, Mass Create - no 6+ powers of spirit demigods here). And off the human goes, to change the world, to burn their passions into its fabric.<br /> <br /> Which, by the way, they'd better do. Failure to use the Influence - fleeing away from what they wanted to do, deciding better, second thoughts leading to want to give the blessing back, just sitting on it dully and surrendering to sloth and inaction - oh, that won't go down well. The shaman's already paid a price for this, but she'll pay a second if the Influence doesn't actually get used. It hurts. It burns. She starts to bleed Essence, one per hour, and pain staccatos through her nerves. Once she hits 0 Essence, she gains the Shadowlash condition. Orrrr... she can eat the human. A mouthful of flesh from the rejector-of-blessings stops the bleed and the pain immediately, ceases the Ban and shuts the whole blessing off. Eating the whole goddamn ungrateful human gives the shaman the Symbolic Focus condition too.<br /> <br /> \u200bSome shamans dole this shit out like drugs - like really expensive drugs, for high prices. Might be cash, might be goods, but it's usually more esoteric - favours due, sacrifices offered, weird shit that they'll get arrested for. Most human Influence-buyers don't understand the true nature of the shaman who sells them it, don't know it's a wolf-in-sheep's clothing. They know just enough about what they're getting to make a very poor decision and become involved in the darker side of the world. Power's a drug, mind, and some become addicted to it. Better hope they can pay the wolf's tithe each time, though. The comedown from this stuff is a bitch, too; after the blessing fades, spirits of the same Resonance as the Influence consider the human to be Open until a month has passed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-23T14:49:31-08:00","id":1170023,"title":"","content":"It's getting late here, but amongst the presents yet to come: secrets caught in snowflakes, Luna's tears, the fraternity of grit and tar, eating your name, pariah skins, and more besides. I'll work over 'em in the coming days <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-23T15:04:56-08:00","id":1170031,"title":"","content":"OMG!!! These are a great Christmas gift!!!! Thank your sir!!!!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3669-blackheartz","name":"blackheartz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3669_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-23T18:04:46-08:00","id":1170053,"title":"","content":"Yarr, this time, I be voting on option 1.<br /> <br /> <br /> Edit: Ohhh, too late. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-23T23:50:58-08:00","id":1170103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1169612-eleven-shaman-blessings?p=1169987#post1169987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Storm Lords do their best to forge agreements with the nobles of darkness and ice so that none will take the open vessel of the sacrifice. Such spirits tend to levy a painful price in some other way.</div> </div> </div> </div>It seems... strange... that Storm Lords would entertain using this rite at all. It acknowledges their weakness against the elements, entreats a spirit to tend to their weakness, and brings into being one of the most dangerous prey, another anathema claimed walking the physical world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-24T00:38:40-08:00","id":1170113,"title":"","content":"I think ideally they would try to bargain to keep that from happening like it says. But it does seem more like the rite is a way to sort of do some Judo on the Winter, turning its cold to your strength, shifting the focus of the spirits to, ideally, something beneficial. I imagine the Storm Lords would try to raise people who would willingly sacrifice themselves in case the others have need of it, but still it might be more popular among other tribes. And if you were having trouble with Winter spirits it offers some strong defense.<br /> <br /> Our game's been having problems with a lingering and pressing cold front created by supernatural things that are theorized to have caused ice ages. I wasn't even done reading before I was pondering how to find a Winter King to sacrifice.<br /> <br /> I like the image of a bunch of stoic Storm Lord stereotypes sitting around a table gruffly encouraging someone to eat, drink and tell them what they want most in life.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/6LeiWOX.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> From Manly Guys Doing Manly Things</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 12-24-2017, 03:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-24T00:59:18-08:00","id":1170116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1169612-eleven-shaman-blessings?p=1170103#post1170103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems... strange... that Storm Lords would entertain using this rite at all. It acknowledges their weakness against the elements, entreats a spirit to tend to their weakness, and brings into being one of the most dangerous prey, another anathema claimed walking the physical world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Better would work as Bone Shadows Rite here?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-24T08:03:49-08:00","id":1170175,"title":"","content":"Well, that digital plague trick is plain awesome. The &quot;shaman drug dealer&quot; is also good, but the digital bless/curse have felt much more &quot;shocking&quot;, especially when you take into account the way it influence other supernaturals-<br /> <br /> Vampire: &quot;how the hell a strix possessed my <i>computer</i>?&quot;<br /> Mage: &quot;and you thought that the new Taylor Swift's song was an earworm..&quot; (burning the brand new abyssal iPod touch)<br /> Promethean: (after escaping the tenth date with an alchemist) &quot;I think my Tinder is trying to kill me&quot;<br /> Changeling: &quot;Siri! I told you to find me an italian restaurant! Not to call every f***g huntsman in a radius of a 100 mile!&quot;<br /> Lucifuge: &quot;I think my iPad has just became a gateway to hell.. again&quot;<br /> Sin Eater: &quot;wait- did my VR headset has just transported me into the middle of a Dead Dominion?.. <i>awesome</i>&quot;<br /> Mummy: &quot;I knew humanity has advanced while I slept- but not &quot;creating a Blue ray player which tries to eat me&quot; level of advanced&quot;<br /> Demon: &quot;So you are saying that it wasn't the God Machine which had made my laptop to try and assassinate me in my sleep? Well, that's a relief&quot;<br /> Beast: &quot;ok, ah ah, funny. Now before I get really pissed- who the hell had decorated my Lair with pop ups of midget porn?!&quot;<br /> Deviant: &quot;I told you that 9GAG is a part of the conspiracy, but nobody listened to me...&quot;<br /> Sin Eater: &quot;wait- where is Wolfi?&quot;<br /> Vampire:&quot;..... that son of a bitch...&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":503,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","user":"LostLight","date":". 12-24-2017, 11:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-24T08:27:35-08:00","id":1170184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1169612-eleven-shaman-blessings?p=1170103#post1170103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It seems... strange... that Storm Lords would entertain using this rite at all. It acknowledges their weakness against the elements, entreats a spirit to tend to their weakness, and brings into being one of the most dangerous prey, another anathema claimed walking the physical world.</div> </div> </div> </div>My thoughts exactly. It screams Hunters in Darkness though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-26T06:12:38-08:00","id":1170659,"title":"","content":"I'll get to answering peoples' comments when I get a moment - just managed to get this one ready before more family have rolled up and need socialising with <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> \u200bIgnore the names for now, then, and focus on what else lies within. A fragment of something hard, something a little tarry; a lump of asphalt and grit from the road. It appears to be spattered with dried blood.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Fellowship Of Tar And Grit</span></b><br /> Post-industrial roads have become an extremely dangerous place in the spirit world. The thundering, clattering, squelching spirits of wheel and transport are aggressive and fast. Even the spirits of the asphalt underfoot are resentful of those who would exploit their bodies' bones and flesh without paying due respect. Most Uratha figure it's safer to keep off the roads when one can and cross them as quickly as possible; after all, quite a few of the things that crawl or race along them are bound not to leave the roads' limits. That said, a shaman who gains the favour of the bubbling tar-matrons of the road courts, or who bargains for secrets of the heaving chaos of traffic from lesser entities of fume and gear, can learn a few useful tricks.<br /> <br /> Roads like blood, because they are rivers of carnage. Throw a track of pitch and grit down and run large, heavy lumps of metal along it at high speeds, and things get killed. Animal roadkill gets ground into the road surface, a sacrifice pulverised again and again on the altar of tar. Humans are caught by the cages of metal, or slam them into each other, and pour their blood onto the ground. Even the constant, tiny, petty deaths of insects slapped against glass and metal hide over and over and over again, each just a minute drop of ichor, are taken as offerings. Their little endings add over time, each a grain of sand that fills an immense cup of arthropod slaughter. The roads drink it all up regardless.<br /> <br /> A shaman who convinces a road court to make a covenant likely finds the spirits' price takes this sort of form. Only the most bloodthirsty courts, crazed by an eternal churn of traffic and human passage and pain and smoke, demand actual human sacrifice. Most need an offering of at least a large animal slain on the asphalt, and then occasional obligations over time like ensuring bonemeal is added to the freshly prepared grit of newly repaired road.<br /> <br /> Have your bargain made? Come to an understanding with the cracked ribs and tarry cartilage of the spirit-road? Step onto the street you've made a bargain with, then, and kneel down close to the asphalt. Feel grit and tar under your hand - let the connection form. Cut the palm, press it down, and let the blood flow. The spirit will drink - a point of Essence, guzzled down as the crimson fluid spills on the ground. Now you and your pack can walk the road with the spirit's aid for a little while. In the Shadow, the predators of steel and smoke will ignore you as they go about their daily struggles; it won't protect you if you deliberately get in their way and provoke them, or if they're specifically out to get you for some reason, but you can avoid unneccessary dangers. Most spirit-roads can't help but be faster to travel than the rest of the spirit-world just by their nature, offering Uratha anything up to +5 to Speed while astride them and heading to a journey's destination (just crossing the road doesn't bestow anything), so being able to navigate with less concern for the metal beasts of the highway can be convenient. In the Flesh, the first accident that would befall you is shunted onto some hapless nearby human instead. Some Iron Masters go on pilgrimages, spirit-quests on the roads, just walking on and on, spilling blood and feeding spirits as they go, living with the road and from it. These pilgrims breath engine fumes and eat roadkill at the edge of the asphalt - or the occasional human furious with road-rage or aroused by the notion of indulging brutal passions on what they think is just a luckless hitchhiker.<br /> <br /> The road-blessing is a good trick for prowling your territory more safely, but there's another that's a bit more practical for getting from A to B quickly. Sometimes an Uratha requires transport sharpish, and taxi drivers are either absent or have an alarming tendency not to take well to a werewolf's needs or behaviour. But mundane, real taxis are just a part of the greater, symbolic whole, the notion of the network of taxis and drivers and transport that threads through the fabric of the city. In the phone book, find the taxi service that doesn't correspond to any real agency or company operating in the city - you can tell which one it is because part of the name dips briefly into First Tongue, or because when you look at the ad from the corner of your eye, it looks back with inky little orbs of its own, or because it sometimes moves from one page to another. Don't call it - the phone number doesn't go anywhere good, trust me - but rip it out the book, that little scrap of paper. When you need transport? Reach into your pocket, find that little scrap of paper, fold it three times and then cut your thumb; let the blood and a point of Essence soak into it. And voila, give yourself a minute at most before a curious cab rolls up; blacked out driver windows, a number plate that isn't on any registry anywhere, and a no-questions-asked policy. They'll take you - and whatever baggage you've got - anywhere in the city, no money required. The price is a favour down the line; the request will come through for you to move something from one spot in the city to another. It might be to pick up a green rucksack from the park and drop it off outside the courts, or to just ride round and round the metro five times (the something, in this case, being yourself). It all has meaning to the spirits, and it's always best to pay your debts.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-26T09:47:15-08:00","id":1170713,"title":"","content":"Having put away a good half a bottle of very fine quality vodka during the family gathering today, I'm clearly in prime condition for some more writing. Let's delve into something with a bit of a kick to it....<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> \u200bPut the grit down alongside the other curios, feel its lingering roughness on your fingertips, then look to the next gift from the bag's contents. This one is larger, more ornate; two wolves curled round each other. Their colours are at stark odds. One speaks forth wisdom, an ivory sliver marked with questions and truths. The other... the other intakes, inhales, consumes. The ebon sliver at its mouth marks that it is a devourer, an eater. Where the first twin gives, the second takes. Where the first explores, the second guards. Where the first discovers, the second... <i>culls</i>.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Eat Your Name</span></b><br /> Give up your name, and hide in its shadow. Rip it up, tear the pieces apart, swallow them down. This is not a good feeling, but it'll protect you for now.<br /> <br /> Most Uratha desperate enough to eat their name are looking for a temporary affair, a time-limited deal, a purgatory rather than permanent damnation. That's what we'll look at here. There are other ways - permanent ways - but you're probably not far-gone enough to consider that. Yet.<br /> <br /> So let's look at how you profane your identity, shall we? You're giving up your name because you want protection. It's either fear or conviction driving you to such a drastic step, I'm guessing. You want the nasty slivers of hurt that swim through the world and catch their barbs in the narrative fabric of the <i>who-you-are </i>to just slide off instead. You want to give nothing for their lamprey-maws to snare any purchase on.<br /> <br /> It's not enough to just summon a spirit of darkness or secrets or entropy or annihilation. It's not enough to just find one in its lair in the Shadow. You have to find the right place and the right time, to seal your pact with such a spirit in a place in the Shadow where the light never reaches and where Essence of the right resonance pools thick - a 5-dot locus of such, or one of the Deep Shadow resting places where Death Wolf sometimes pauses in her travels, or one of the strange, Escher-painting tangles of architecture born from the dreams of a stifled architect who could never see their goals made in the stubborn, uncompliant Flesh. You go there and you perform the oblations necessary for that place. There'll be a sacrifice of some sort. There always is.<br /> <br /> How you shed the name depends on the place. You carve or ink it into your flesh, shuck it off in a bloody excision with knife or talon, and feed it to the eager flock of spirits that wait for your benediction with eager hunger. You take all the photos that you own of yourself, and wash them with your blood until your depicted face smears and dissolves. You burn things that matter to you, that are part of who you are. You reject what is central to yourself, the things that are<i> who you are</i>. You speak your name over and over again until it simply loses meaning, until it is a random agglomeration of syllables with no deeper sense to it.<br /> <br /> Pay the congregation of spirits what they desire, which will likely be a deep cost indeed. Pay worship to Death Wolf. Lose yourself in the insane architecture. Become insensate, become less than who you are. This is meditation of a nihilistic fashion, an attempt to scour yourself clean of everything that connects you to the world.<br /> <br /> During this process, the place that you are in and the price you are paying will have very real effects. A scattering of your connections are lost forever, and there's no way to tell who or what beforehand. It won't be one of the People, or one of the Shadowfolk. But the ties will break nonetheless; an ex-lover forgets you forever; an old friend loses touch with finality; a mentor stops fondly remembering you, stops remembering you at all. In the worst cases, the ties that snap are deep and close. A mother forgets her son. A true friend wonders why they ever bothered. An oath born of a saved life is cast aside callously.<br /> <br /> Now, <i>now </i>you are ready for the hunt.<br /> <br /> You call a sacred hunt upon your own name, and you hunt it through the Shadow. It will be a dangerous trip, and when you find it, your name will not necessarily be what you are expecting. It might be whispered in the cascade of a spirit-waterfall, or tossed from beak to beak by a murder of crows. It might glint in the churned earth like a gem, or slink through the grim darkness as an oozing worm. Catch it, take it in your jaws, swallow it down.<br /> <br /> Your name is gone.<br /> <br /> You are made empty. Firstly, Harmony breaks immediately out of balance; it shifts 1 further to Spirit or Flesh, whichever it is closer to. An Uratha at Harmony 5 breaks one way or the other at random. This isn't a roll; it's a break. Secondly, whatever level of Death Rage trigger you suffer, it's now one stage worse for the duration of your namelessness; lacking such an identity to tie the threads of spirit and self together, the spasming foam of Essence and primal inheritance from Urfarah's mantle is loosened and provoked.<br /> <br /> Oh, and of course,<i> the name is gone</i>. You can't remember it anymore. If it is spoken to you, you immediately forget it. Any attempt to give a new name slides off too. The best that can be managed are broad titles - 'you', 'Rahu', 'pack-brother' and the like. You don't forget your ties, but they are harder to draw upon; you suffer a -3 penalty to all rolls that would draw on Allies, Contacts or Status, and you cannot gain new dots in any of these merits. No spirit will honour a debt or favour owed to your earlier name, or consider you in a favourable light due to your actions before consuming your identity; you can build up new relationships in this time, though, even if the spirits will likely see your lack-of-name as a weakness to be exploited. Every day, you must spend a point of Willpower or gain the Madness Condition.<br /> <br /> So what do you get for all this? You prowl the deep Shadow, you tear off who you are and suffer for it, and for what? For namelessness. For reducing yourself to no more than a tumbled stone in the stream of causality, barely registering in the constant flow of existence. You have flayed yourself of who you are, and your caulked blood is a shield.<br /> <br /> Your name is not a valid method or aid for any means of targeting you for as long as it is gone. It does not count as your name in any mundane, symbolic, or metaphysical way. All supernatural attempts to affect or influence you suffer a -5 penalty to their dice pool and dramatically fail on a failure, regardless of if they require your name, unless they have the forceful physicality of a direct attack that deals damage such as a werewolf's claws or a spirit's Blast numen. Mind control slides off, scrabbling for purchase and slipping away. The winds of fate and prophecy cannot see you; stored records or archived information about you has a tendency to suffer and degrade; new records formed about you during this time lack all identifying information. Attempts to recall you based on only minor recollections or encounters suffer a -5 penalty as well. You are a gap in the narrative of the world; the story is not expecting your emergence.<br /> <br /> How long is the name gone? Well, it varies, depending on the exact method you used. It might require you perform a Sacred Hunt and eat the spirit who ate your name. It might require a pilgrimage to places sacred to Death Wolf, to beseech her for its return. Perhaps you must convince a Tribal elder who holds your name etched into the bones of a hero that you are <i>you </i>and not one of the shape-stealing horrors who so eagerly seek to assume the void you have left. Perhaps your name is not where you left it, and you must hunt through the Shadow to find where it has ended up, and hope any new owner is willing to reliquish it. When - if - you finally secure your name again, Harmony immediately breaks out of balance again. Go without your name for a full year, and you gain the persistent Madness condition regardless of your best efforts.<br /> <br /> But even amongst those who know of how to eat their own name, and who judge the dangers a worthy price for a potent advantage and the erosion of the self, there's a reason they are hesitant. Everyone who has eaten their name then vomited it back up knows that there is something <i>else </i>that knows it too. Something is out there, the real dealer in the exchange, something you've offered a vital part of yourself to and that has only returned the name to you bearing the mark of its talons. The Eater of Names is watching you now, and you <i>know </i>it has purpose and intent in its vigil. One day it will come for you, and it will have a duty for you, and your very name will demand you fulfil it. The feeling never goes away, unless you shear off your name forever.<br /> <br /> There's a few strange Bone Shadow shamans who have no names at all, who have made it so they <i>never </i>did, and who can tell you how to take that final step - the greater, true excision of identity, debriding the existence of their person a from the world. That's a topic for another time, I think.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-26T10:56:23-08:00","id":1170730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> These pilgrims breath engine fumes and eat roadkill at the edge of the asphalt - or the occasional human furious with road-rage or aroused by the notion of indulging brutal passions on what they think is just a luckless hitchhiker </div> </div> </div>If I'll ever write a Forsaken fan fiction, it would now definitely start with &quot;a slasher tries to kidnap and murder a lone hitchhiker only to get eaten alive in honor of mother Road&quot; <br /> <br /> Anyway, I really like that portrayal of of roads in the Shadow- really creepy, really awesome. It reminds me some God Machine fiction I read once- but since when the cog head has monopoly over technological horror? The &quot;spirit transporter&quot; company is also great, even though that if I were to use it, I would probably also allow mortals to somehow summon its drivers, even if they have no idea what they are getting into. It just has some great potential for a mortal game, IMO.<br /> <br /> On another note-<br /> <br /> THE EATER OF NAMES IS COMING! SAVE YOURSELF! SAVE YOUR NAMES!<br /> <br /> (seriously, will we ever get a Lodge/ cult/ potential tribe/ anything more about that elusive Firstborn? Because they are awesome).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-27T07:39:30-08:00","id":1170941,"title":"","content":"<br /> Be careful as you place the twin wolves to one side; it doesn't do to upset that pair with careless disrespect. Onto the next trinket, already dangling part-way out of the bag, and tangled with another that lies deeper; this one here is a set of carefully beaten little silver plates, tiny, each the shape of a phase of the moon. Handle gently - it is silver, after all. Not enough here to ignite the Essence in your blood to real intensity, but enough to give a Pure a sting. On each little moon, tiny glyphs glint - names of revered lunes, the titles by which they are to be called and summoned.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Premium Grade Triple-Distilled Lunar Spirit</span></b><br /> Here is a goblet. It is full to the brim with a roiling concoction, all twisting streams of liquid crystal, quicksilver, and carmine fluid. You're going to take this goblet and drink that weird admixture down. It's going to be your new best friend. It is a lunar elemental.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe image that most Uratha get in their heads at the phrase 'lunar elemental' is of a lune. Lunar elementals are quite probably lunes, or made from lunes, but they're also <i>not</i>\u200b lunes; they're quite probably spirits, or very close to such, but they are definitely <i>not</i>\u200b spirits at the same time. Outside of a werewolf's body, any given lunar elemental is just a squirming knot of fluid mass; it is physical and manifest in both Flesh and Shadow. Without the fire of an Uratha's Essence channels to give it animation and purpose, it doesn't <i>do</i>\u200b anything apart from stir with some semblance of sluggish life from time to time. Spirits shy away from attempting to consume such an aberrant being. If left dormant for long enough, an elemental will slowly shrivel up and evaporate, but that takes a <i>very</i> long time.<br /> <br /> \u200bTales about as to how lunar elementals come about. They bleed from the wounds of the Warden Moon's flesh as she shatters leviathans of the void in battle, and lunes reverently collect some of the gore of their goddess. They are the tears of a Luna who is not real, a weeping Warden of an alternate reality where the world below is a broken apocalypse, and the weight of a divinity's grief is enough to seep through the seams of this adjacent existence from time to time. There is a factory, somewhere, where they bind lunes and grind them down for all manner of ephemeral produce, from dark powders that burn with brilliant flames of moonlight when ignited to draughts of lune-lymph that ward against curses and, of course the elemental stuff derived from the core of the spirit's self-identity. There's a brewery where lunes imbue the gurgling, dripping tubes and vats with so much lunar Essence that it bubbles out and slithers around, self-animating. A chunk of the moon was shattered off by an impact in aeons past and fell to earth, a piece of the Warden's flesh, now buried deep underground where it struck the earth; veins of god-gore sometimes dribble up into the Shadow's light. When an Uratha makes a greater lune feel true reverence or deep, all-encompassing love, the spirit vomits up an ephemeral child of elemental moon-meat. The ancestors of great Uratha are carried up to the moon to do battle with the terrors of the greater dark and, when they die a second time, their void-riddled spirit-carcasses slough off these elemental cankers from the parts of their defiance and rage that refuse to give up the battle even then. There's any number of other stories too. Lunar elementals are so rare that there's little common ground to connect the various times they have been discovered, been given as gifts by lunes, or appeared in other ways. What matters is what they <i>do</i>.<br /> <br /> An Uratha who drinks an elemental will activate it; contact with the werewolf's Essence brings it to life immediately. From then on, the elemental dwells within the werewolf's flesh, a familiar trapped in a prison of its masters flesh, bone and blood. If the werewolf dies, so does the elemental. It might be possible to extract an elemental through clever Essence alchemy or nightmarish surgical procedures, but the being cannot extract itself voluntarily.<br /> <br /> \u200bAs well as the occasional uncomfortable tug, shift or pulse within the body, the Uratha can feel the elemental's presence as a vague presence at the edge of awareness - a tingle or fizz in the neurones of the brain and the fabric of the soul. The lunar elemental weaves itself into the connection between werewolf and Warden Moon - the auspice itself. If imbibed by a werewolf without a lunar Auspice, an elemental will rapidly go mad and toxic.<br /> <br /> \u200bA werewolf with a lunar Auspice and a lunar elemental can, instead of using their normal auspice ability, use one of the following powers once per chapter instead:<ul><li>The werewolf's natural weapons ooze with a slick, metallic venom for 2 rounds, inflicting the grave Poison tilt on any enemies injured.</li> <li>The werewolf's regenerative abilities erupt into a hyperactive state, increasing the levels of damage healed each round by 5 for 2 rounds.</li> <li>The werewolf's flesh liquefies and becomes formless, creating limbs, pseudopods, eyes or other body parts as needed. In this form, the werewolf has +2 Strength and Stamina, can slide through gaps of any size, climb walls and cling to ceilings, can manifest Gauru claws and jaws, has any number of limbs required and is unaffected by Tilts; the werewolf also gains a +3 bonus to grapple checks and triggers Lunacy as if in Gauru form. This form can be maintained for a number of rounds equal to 3 + the werewolf's Stamina + Primal Urge.</li> </ul>\u200bAdditionally, a lunar elemental will immediately alert an Uratha if she intakes any sort of poisonous or toxic substance, whether physical or supernatural in nature.<br /> <br /> \u200bA lunar elemental is relatively low-maintenance - it requires a single point of Essence per week from the werewolf's pool to sustain itself. However, it also adds a very distinct element to the werewolf's scent. Attempts to track or locate the Uratha via scent or spiritual senses benefit from a +3 bonus, and creatures that are particularly attuned to the mystic qualities of blood can immediately detect the Uratha's unusual nature in close proximity.<br /> <br /> \u200bWerewolves that lack a lunar auspice often end up with poisoned flesh (inflicting the Poison tilt on those that bite them or are splashed with their blood), horribly warped flesh (a permanent increase to regenerative capabilities, but at the cost of a permanently, obviously monstrous appearance), and a reaction to silver that's positively incendiary, enough to set nearby creatures and objects aflame from the heat that spills from such injuries. Alarmingly, there's a few tales where a hapless Pure arrogant enough to think it could control the chaotic energy of a lunar elemental's bond ended up both mutated and also capable of vomiting up new, corrupted elementals into the meat of other werewolves that it managed to bite, copying its affliction to its victims in a blood-born plague of moon-tainted horror.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-27T08:32:26-08:00","id":1170954,"title":"","content":"Past the chain of tiny silver moons is something else - a spirit-braid. Pull the thread out of the bag, and with it come the little charms tied to its length - little symbolic representations of spirit choirs, each carefully sculpted so that the shaman can feel the lessons of its surface just with fingertips. Each notch, each bump, each carved mark is a mnemonic reminder of a ban, or a bane - of a law, or a crime - of something relating to that choir and its members, of something that can protect against them, or be used as a lever to influence them with.<br /> <br /> \u200bNot every shaman can keep every scrap of detail in their head. It can be handy to have a little reminder, when dealing with spirits.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">\u200bThe Lion's Paw</span></b><br /> The shaman's task in shepherding the Shadow isn't just about slaughtering hostile spirits and littering the <i>Hisil</i>\u200b with their ephemeral viscera. Sometimes, a touch more care is required; assuming that one can make <i>friends</i>\u200b with all the dwellers of the reflected world is a fool's errand, but alliances can be forged, catastrophes averted and harmony spread through the right application of protection or healing at the right time. In some places, spiritual blights slither through the Shadow, prompted by <i>idigam</i>\u200b or Bale Hounds or simply born from grotesque but natural phenomena; the cycles of the <i>Hisil</i>\u200b can be set off course by the undesired defeat of a keystone spirit and set matters spiralling into chaos; a wounded ally might be a great asset if not for the horrific injuries it has suffered. The shaman, then, isn't just the wolf who culls the flock and kills the weak so that the whole may be stronger; they are the shepherd who looks ahead beyond simple, immediate and primal hungers for the hunt and the prey, planning with wisdom the careful balancing of the twin worlds they strive to maintain.<br /> <br /> \u200bEven for those who do not attempt to sculpt the Shadow's currents through the application of such mercies, concern for more immediate spirit allies and, indeed, the pack totem can mean that rites which allow them to heal and aid spiritual beings are of significant value.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Heal Spirit (Pack Rite \u2022\u2022)</b></span><br /> This rite draws ambient power directly from the Hisil around the ritemaster, weaving threads into the substance of a wounded spirit to reinforce its symbolic strength directly.<br /> <br /> <b>Symbols:</b> Blood, healing, water, fire.<br /> <br /> <b>Action:</b> Extended (10 successes; each roll represents five minutes)<br /> <br /> <b>Success:</b> This ritual targets a single spirit, which must either be willing or be bound by another rite. At the rite's culmination, the ritemaster may heal any number of points of lethal damage to the spirit's corpus, spending 2 Essence per point to do so. In balance, a participating pack member suffers an additional -1 wound penalty for the remainder of the scene.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Cleanse Spirit (Pack Rite \u2022</b><b>\u2022\u2022</b><b>\u2022)</b></span><br /> This rite draws upon old, powerful echoes of primeval balance underpinning the Shadow's nature.<br /> <br /> <b>Symbols:</b> Blood, purification, water, fire.<br /> <br /> <b>Action:</b> Extended (15 successes; each roll represents five minutes); potentially penalised by the Rank of a spiritual source of the Conditions or effects<br /> <br /> <b>Success:</b> This ritual targets a single spirit, which must either be willing or be bound by another rite. At the rite's culmination the spirit is purified of a negative Condition, and any supernatural effects on it that alter its attributes, nature, or Essence are purged. In balance, a pack member suffers a moderate Sick Tilt for the remainder of the scene. This rite can only remove the taint of a Maeljin from a spirit that is Rank 1 or 2; more potent spirits require greater and likely more unique methods of purification, if they can be purged of the Wounds' taint at all. Removing the taint of a Maeljin also inflicts the Madness condition on the Sick pack member for the scene's duration.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Gird Spirit (Pack Rite \u2022)</span></b><br /> This rite lends some of the symbolic strength of a pack's close ties to a spirit, girding it with Essence.<br /> <br /> <b>Symbols:</b> Shielding, the pack, loyalty, metal or earth.<br /> <br /> \u200b<b>Cost:</b> 1 Essence per spirit.<br /> <br /> <b>Action:</b> Extended (5 successes; each roll represents one minute)<br /> <br /> <b>Success:</b> This ritual targets one or more spirits, which must either be willing or be bound by another rite. At the rite's culmination, the ritemaster expends a point of Essence per spirit thus affected, reinforcing each spirit with this energy. Affected spirits gain a single point of armour, add a single point of damage to their attacks, and gain +2 to their resistance when opposing supernatural effects. A spirit may also immediately expend the girding to grant a Clash of Wills against a supernatural effect. The spirits do not gain any of these benefits against the ritemaster or members of the ritemaster's pack, however, and the spirit's appearance is altered to indicate allegiance to the pack in some way, such as depicting the pack's symbol, gaining wolf-like masks of spirit-matter, or changing colours and hues to match those of the pack. Additionally, a girded spirit cannot willingly pay allegiance or swear vassalhood to another spirit unless it is the pack's totem, and cannot be <i>forced</i>\u200b to pay allegiance or become a vassal for the rite's duration. Acting in a way that serves loyalty to the pack or the totem can restore 1 point of Willpower to the spirit once per story. Unless expended to force a Clash of Wills, each spirit will receive the benefits of girding for a month.<br /> <br /> \u200bThere are probably several much more potent Tribal forms of this rite, each attuned to the power and portfolio of one of the Firstborn and imbuing a spirit with a fragment of the patron's power.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>\u200bMask Spirit (Wolf Rite \u2022\u2022\u2022)</b></span><br /> The ritemaster shrouds a spirit by tearing away part of its surface symbolism, drinking the sheared-off identity down to hide it from prying eyes.<br /> <br /> \u200b<b>Symbols: </b>Jaws, concealment, darkness, chains<br /> <br /> <b>Cost:</b> 5 Essence<br /> <br /> \u200b<b>Action:</b> Extended (10 successes; each roll represents 1 turn)<br /> <br /> \u200b<b>Success:</b> This rite targets a single spirit, which must be either willing or bound by another rite. At the culmination of the rite the ritemaster consumes a portion of the spirit's identity, dealing it a single point of aggravated damage; the ritemaster gains the Ban Condition matching the spirit's Ban. For the duration of the rite's effects, the spirit's footprint in the world is reduced both physically and spiritually. The rite imposes a -3 penalty on all attempts to track, locate or perceive the spirit unless it is actively hostile and attempting to attack; by spending a Willpower point, the spirit can force a failure on any such roll to become a Dramatic Failure. Other spirits will assume it is a minor or irrelevant spirit of no interest to them unless it directly attracts their attention or intervenes with their activities; this effect can be overcome by spending a Willpower point, but most spirits will have no reason to do so. Attempts to detect its Ban or Bane will, if successful, answer with the ritemaster's Bane of silver and any Ban Conditions the ritemaster is under instead of those of the spirit. The rite's effects last until the next full moon; the spirit cannot heal the aggravated damage from the rite until it ends.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-27T09:36:23-08:00","id":1170973,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Words Of An Oak</span></b><br /> Young lovers carve their initials in the trunk of an old oak tree. Children growing to objectionable recklessness scrawl rough declamations of their enemies and pronunciations of their own inevitable rule into the bark with their sharp little knives. Self-proclaimed worshippers of the wild amble out of their comfortable lives for a brief dance around the tree in vain hope of finding spiritual succor. The humans don't understand the true nature of the ancient oak that they briefly bind into their lives. They can't really see the depths of its age, the glacially slow contemplation of its Shadow sentience, or the wisdom its boughs sift from the sky and draw up from the earth. They certainly have no idea of what a total bastard your average oak really is.<br /> <br /> Oak trees have the gift of prophecy. Half-asleep oak spirits can prognosticate and predict with surprising eloquence, when the fancy takes them. They're better at perceiving the slow currents of change - how a city's expansion will resculpt the landscape and how its growing communities will clash or intertwine with each other, how a government will stumble and fall, how a revolution will slowly build before its inevitable flashfire into incendiary tumult, how an elder Uratha's arrogance will bring about her doom. Still, they're reasonably on the ball when it comes to particularly local events - an oak can accurately predict the time and cause of death of a human who lives within one mile if it will happen in the next year, right down to the day, hour and even minute. An oak can see whose jealousies will burst into flame and how the raging fire of hatred and bitterness will consume households and families. An oak knows where the body will be buried, and who will dance with joy at the downfall of another. Oaks rarely prophecy or even consider pleasant, good things - or just practical and useful concepts like the next week's lottery numbers - and this is because they seethe with their own bitter envies and sour unhappiness. An oak spirit that manages to achieve serenity, harmony or peace loses its ability to prophecy.<br /> <br /> Oak spirits lie a lot. They can only utter prophecy when at least semi-dormant, and always demand a price for their services but are somehow capable of uttering falsehood even if they swear oaths and accept gathra for the bargain. How and why oak spirits are capable of violating the sanctity of the transaction isn't clear, but may stem back to transgressions in some past, primeval aeon.<br /> <br /> Oaks like to lie because they can use their twisted prophecies to bring about ruin and doom for the people they mislead. On the other hand, if they always lied, even the wise and cautious shamans would never trust them, so the oaks know they must sometimes speak the genuine truth to maintain some semblance of value to their prognostications.<br /> <br /> A prophecy can only be elicited once a year, and then only from the eldest oak in the region. The price is cheap enough for an Uratha, but others who would glean the wisdom of the trees have to swear to perform a duty in service to the oak; wise bargainers get the details on a task before they make the agreement, rather than leaving it open to the oak's malice down the line. Failure to carry out the duty will result in the spirit world turning against the transgressor, plaguing them with ill fortune and supernatural malisons; this is the case even if the oak's prophecy was a lie.<br /> <br /> Accomplished shamans use the performance of the rite as an opportunity to manipulate the dormant spirit as it comes to full wakefulness for the prophecy, using the full extent of their wiles and cleverness to try and convince the oak to tell the truth rather than a falsehood. Blood offerings are a very effective way to quickly improve the impression that an oak has of the ritemaster; in a few distant corners of supposedly civilised lands, lone travellers have a tendency to disappear when the locals water the roots of a revered, sacred oak with fresh blood for the yearly festival.<br /> <br /> \u200bThere is one last wrinkle to the oaks and their prophecy, a scrap of lore so obtuse that only a tiny number of shaman know it to be the case. There are, from time to time, stories of beings wrought from lightning and metal; servants of strange powers indeed. Should such an angelic messenger give orders to an oak spirit, it can force the spirit to utter whatever the messenger desires in place of the augury that would usually spill forth. In this way, these beings can - on the incredibly rare occasions they appear - conscript the sacred oaks and prophetic wood-shrines of some human cults to serve their own manipulative purposes.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Oak Prophecy (Pack Rite \u2022)</b></span><br /> Old pacts with spirits of the wood can stir a slumbering oak spirit to brief wakefulness, granting it the ability to utter a prophecy.<br /> <br /> <b>Symbols:</b> Oak, bright colours, dancing, awakening<br /> <br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1 Essence (Uratha) or a promised favour or duty (everyone else)<br /> <br /> <b>Action:</b> Extended (5 successes, each roll represents half an hour)<br /> <br /> <b>Success:</b> This rite can only be performed once a year, and only at the oldest oak in a region. At the rite's culmination, the tree's spirit awakens and grants a prophecy, manifesting briefly through the creaking of the tree's boughs and the cracking of its bark. If the ritemaster has asked for a prophecy on a particular topic, the spirit will do so if the topic is something that is within its remit. If simply asked for a prophecy without specifics, it will prophecy on something relating to the ritemaster or other participants in the rite; it might predict the death of a loved one, or warn of a coming doom, or reveal a threat that exists and which the ritemaster is not aware of. However, there is an equal chance that the prophecy will be true, or be a lie; if the spirit's social impression of the ritemaster is Excellent due to leverage, gifts, or other efforts on the ritemaster's part, the odds of a true prophecy increase to two-thirds, and if the impression is perfect it rises to three-quarters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-27T11:30:31-08:00","id":1171002,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Pariah Skin</b></span><br /> Why take the blame, when you can shuffle the consequences off onto someone else?<br /> <br /> It's an old theme in spiritual and religious practices. Hand your sin off to another. Make an effigy onto which a disaster or curse can be shifted. Convince the evil spirits to infest the livestock instead of you, then kill the animals. Anchor the fuck-ups you've made to your home, then torch it and walk away as your past links symbolically go up in flame. It's all about shedding your skin so that the karmic vengeance strikes an empty husk, or better still, getting some other poor bugger to wear the skin for you.<br /> <br /> Amongst Uratha shaman, the common parlance usually names such techniques - the ones that are made real by the Shadow and the power of Essence - as 'pariah skins', symbolic scapegoats serving as lightning rods for the occult shit the world tries to throw and for the crimes the shaman commits in the line of duty. There's three broad categories of pariah skin - a literal mantle or coat of skin that the shaman wears, dolls or effigies, and living animals.<br /> <br /> It's rather grotesque, but a pariah mantle is a cloak, coat or other covering made of flayed skin. For once, the process of making one doesn't involve ripping it off some poor victim; for the pariah magic to work, it has to be the user's own skin. For an Uratha, this means an agonising process that will inflict several levels of lethal damage as it is performed; thankfully regeneration makes the notion viable at all. The skin has to then be treated, marked with the correct glyphs and invocations, then donned ceremonially; it doesn't need to be outwardly visible, though, and the thin Uratha-leather garment can be easily hidden under clothes. When it works, the skin seethes and smokes for as long as its power can hold out, after which it rapidly crispens and crumples away.<br /> <br /> Pariah effigies are simple and relatively easy to produce in numbers, although they're also anchored to a location. These draw on symbolic links that the shaman must imbue between themselves and the doll; some make little figurines that represent them, or weave in pieces of their own hair or bone, or build a mad little wooden or lacquered pantheon depicting spirits of secrecy and misdirection which they anoint in their own blood. When used to protect the shaman from a malison, an effigy will smoke and crumble to ash, or crack violently, or start to gibber before sloughing flesh-like layers off and expiring amidst its own false viscera.<br /> <br /> A pariah animal is simply that - a living beast used as the shaman's stand-in. A pig, chicken, rat or other small creature is common. Patterns of warding and false-scripture declaring the animal to be the shaman are marked on its hide; some shaman use paints and pigments, but since the markings need to be intact for the magic to work, more turn to brands, scarification and other permanent approaches to the problem. When the symbolic link brings down doom upon the hapless animal, sometimes the beast suffers whatever fate lay in wait for the shaman; other times the creature simply catches aflame, or hemorrages violently and swiftly.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Pariah Skin (\u2022\u2022\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b></span><br /> \u200b<br /> \u200b<b>Prerequisites:</b> Occult 4, Resolve 3, must be Uratha or Wolf-Blooded<br /> <br /> \u200b<b>Effects:</b> Your character has learned the profane arts of the pariah skin, and knows the occult secrets required to make the world believe a scapegoat stand-in is symbolically you. Once per story, when your character would be affected by a hostile supernatural effect that is not a direct attack that deals damage, your character may reflexively enter a Clash of Wills against the effect with the dice pool using the character's highest Renown. Your character does not need to be aware of the supernatural effect occurring to use this protection. If the Clash is successful, the source will not be aware that the effect has been negated; instead, it will be given the impression that the effect has worked successfully.<br /> <br /> At \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u200b, your character immediately becomes aware of the hostile attempt when it happens, and understands something of the nature of its source if it would not be immediately evident; you can identify the broad type of effect, such as a spirit's Numina, a Facet, etc. The source becomes a valid target for a tracking attempt; your character can follow the threads of symbolic power as clearly as if they were a strong scent.<br /> <br /> <b>Drawback: </b>The protection of the pariah skin is based on a physical thing, which can be destroyed or disrupted. A mantle can be torn away, a collection of effigies knocked over or wrecked, and an animal killed.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-27T13:53:46-08:00","id":1171051,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Sea Dogs</b></span><br /> Bear with me on this one. I'm going to drop largely out of narrative or characterful writing here, because it's late, I'm tired and I'm running out of brain juice. I want to talk for a moment about the process behind getting to the end result (or indeed, getting anywhere) with this entry.<br /> <br /> \u200bI made up a bit list of ideas and concepts when starting to tackle this thread, and have been working through it, grabbing one bit or another and writing, rewriting, hacking things apart and writing again. Normally I'd do a lot more drafts and refinements still, but this is meant to be a bit of fun and it'd be nice to get it done at least vaguely within the perimeters of the Christmas holiday season. Having thinned the list down a lot by the time we've reached this point - this entry being number 10 - I had 'something naval/maritime' on the roster still. Someone on Discord mentioned they wanted to see something for the sea, so hey, I thought, handy convergence.<br /> <br /> \u200bThen I sort of flailed around a bit, because I wasn't particularly sure <i>what</i>\u200b to do. I started thinking about the problems sea wolves have to deal with - the issues with being on a cramped ship while a potential berserker engine of death, the problems with the weather and the fact the ocean is a hungry, dangerous place spiritually, and of course the concern of the vessel itself. It's always an issue with supernatural stuff where there are lots of ways to tamper or damage technological things and structures - the most vulnerable point in a shipful of werewolves is the ship. A lot of supernatural abilities and powers can do a number on a ship quite easily, and potent foes can just tear a hole in it.<br /> <br /> \u200bProblem was, following this line of thinking, I ended up getting mired in defensive, no-sell concepts, which I dislike. What I mean is, looking at ways that werewolves can strengthen their ship and stop it getting trashed, or ways to tamp down on Kuruth problems on a long voyage. Thing is, there's already possibilities covered in these areas - Uratha have the normal set of Death Rage management tools still, and if you want to look at a way to protect a ship from supernatural tampering, take a gander at the Nomad Chain from the Thousand Steel Teeth in The Pack and adapt a version of it for ships (call it something funky like the Albatross Burden or make it a figurehead or something). With eating your own name and pariah skins already being highly defensive, protective measures in this thread, I want to take a different tack.<br /> \u200b<br /> \u200bThe storms and spirits and that sort of danger are pretty nifty too, but while having a crack at that, I hit a creativity doldrum. I had a notion about bottling weather up to boost rites or control the weather, but a werewolf can already use the Elements and Weather Gifts, summon spirits to do stuff, and generally the ideas I was coming up with were overlapping too heavily with these existing concepts. Still, this is the thread for shamanic stuff, and I definitely felt like something rites or occultism-related should lie at the core.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe other problem here is that we don't really have any meaningful framework for seagoing ventures, and I don't plan to write up an entire naval system off the cuff for this one entry.<br /> <br /> \u200bAnyway, after banging these ideas around in my head for a while and ending up feeling frustrated at what I'd written, a few core points rolled out. Something for a ritemaster, yes. But also, refocus this on the central plank we pursued in Forsaken 2e - the notion that werewolves are hunters and predators. What's really cool about having wolves on the waves? The pursuit, the chase, the hunt. So rather than fiddling around with what I was angling for earlier, why not something that helps make the ritemaster on the waves into the consummate predator of the tides? Why not focus on a bit of material that amps up the ritemaster's capabilities as a pursuer on the sea, wielding rites and occult power?<br /> <br /> \u200bShaking <i>that</i>\u200b around my head a while longer resulted in it solidifying into a style merit, which follows. I still don't guarantee excellence, and of course we still don't have a solid naval framework to be hanging it off, but hopefully it gets at the main idea. Please excuse the lack of descriptive text!<br /> \u200b<br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Tide Hunter (Style Merit, \u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022)</b></span><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Occult 4, Resolve 3, at least 5 dots of rites<br /> \u200b<br /> <b>Storm Rider (\u2022\u200b): </b>While aboard a vessel, your character halves the time on extended action rolls to conjure and bind weather spirits and elementals. When weather spirits or elementals that your character has summoned or bargained with are aiding the ship with their Influences, characters attempting to navigate or steer the vessel benefit from the 8-again quality on their dice pools for such purposes.<br /> <br /> <b>Wave Chaser (\u2022\u2022\u200b):</b> While aboard a vessel, when your character invokes the Sacred Hunt rite against another vessel, your ship only loses a pursuit roll against that vessel if the prey achieves an exceptional success on the dice; a normal success is treated as the prey losing the contest by 2 instead.<br /> <br /> <b>Blood And Salt (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u200b):</b> When your character uses the Hunting Ground rite to declare a vessel their sanctified territory, then when pursuing, attacking or boarding another vessel, when prey's blood is spilt on either your vessel's deck or that of the enemy, you no longer need to pay the Essence cost to cause your character's regeneration to heal lethal damage for the remainder of the scene. Furthermore, any of the preys' dice pools of supernatural powers that would heal damage, restore health or ease pain suffer a -3 penalty for the remainder of the scene.<br /> <br /> \u200bI can see space for a 4-dot capstone here that potentially varies in effect depending on the ritemaster's Tribe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-27T14:26:13-08:00","id":1171058,"title":"","content":"...my intended final blessing was going to be something a bit silly, but it seems to be mutating into a more solid idea, so I'll come back to it once it's settled into a coherent and viable form!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-27T14:33:50-08:00","id":1171059,"title":"","content":"Good one <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-27T14:50:26-08:00","id":1171064,"title":"","content":"Awesome finally some water adventures. Really like the use of sorcery styles and styles beyond combat like in Secrets of the Covenants. Blood and Salt is gonna be wicked to use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-27T16:35:57-08:00","id":1171089,"title":"","content":"I wonder if there is any promise in a &quot;treat the vessel as the Uratha&quot; Rite. Just general Gift boosts or crazy &quot; my galleon enters Death Rage/Gauru Form&quot;?<br /> <br /> EDIT: I'm also really looking forward to Fiiiive Pounds of Meat!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 12-27-2017, 07:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-28T03:50:38-08:00","id":1171193,"title":"","content":"Blood and Salt is wicked.<br /> <br /> I am loving all these, but Pariah Skin, Eat Your Name and Oak Prophecy are my absolute favourites. Damm Oaks, man...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-28T09:44:42-08:00","id":1171250,"title":"","content":"The lunar elementals are really cool, and I may even have the company which distill lunes into them (unless those are Cheiron. Or the Hototogisu. Or Amalgama. Or Daeva. Or Last Dynasties. Or Whiteheart. Yeah, we have a lot of potential candidates for this). I wonder what would happen to regular humans who drink them- the easy answer would be &quot;same as the Pure, more or less&quot;, but I think there are cooler options out there.<br /> <br /> The Oak Prophecy thing is also really great. Loved the God Machine reference- makes me think what leverage does it have to force those ancient, spiteful spirits to its command. I also feel like I should know why oaks can lie in their prophesies, but I can't put the finger on it- which is a good thing. Loved that they are presented in a way which is so drastically different from the cultural representations of oaks- that is, of old, smart and generous trees. I wonder if other tree spirits would have similar quirks, which sounds kinda cool, IMO.<br /> <br /> Pariah skin sounds like a classic trick which simply makes sense in the context. As for Sea Dogs, I must say that I've liked to read your thought process as much as I liked reading your fluffy writeups- you should describe those, from time to time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-30T09:58:31-08:00","id":1171817,"title":"","content":"This one banged back and forth round my skull for a while; as I said, it started rather as a joke, and I really, <i>really</i>\u200b cannot vouch for any semblance of game balance to this one in particular. Note that it could be done quite a few other ways as well - as one or more rites, as a Blood Talon Tribal blessing from the Firstborn or something, etc etc. I ran it in this particular format in the end as it allows me to tier and thus add in all the many effects I was considering - a rite should probably be simpler, like the human/Wolf-Blooded merit version is, to make it easier to run.<br /> <br /> \u200bInfinite Rage is quite fun. I like the notion of a last-standing werewolf being utterly annihilated, disintegrated, or otherwise eradicated by something really horrifically heavyweight like an idigam and then <i>still</i>\u200b regenerating itself back together to keep fighting - bones and muscle and sinew rethreading themselves out of the dust and the air, pushed on by a rage that even death isn't enough to stop. <div align=\"left\"><br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">The Inverse Werewolf Law, or, Conservation Of Rage</span></b></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">When a werewolf gets hurt, it gets angrier.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\">When the pack gets hurt, it gets angrier.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Fewer pack members standing just means more fury concentrated in those that remain.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Don\u2019t get angry. Don\u2019t get even. Get angry <i>and</i> get even.</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Rising Fury (Style, \u2022\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</span></span></b></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><b>Prerequisites:</b> Resolve 3, Occult 2, Primal Urge 2</span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Your character is closely attuned to the pain and fury of their pack. The wounds of their comrades only drive them to greater heights of rage.</span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">For the purposes of this merit, pack members count as defeated if they are dead, unconscious, incapacitated or incapable of continuing to currently participate in the combat due to enemy actions (so a pack member entangled by a plant spirit\u2019s Numina and this incapable of reaching anyone to attack would count as incapable); pack members count as gravely wounded if they have suffered aggravated damage due to enemy activity.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><b>Rage Cascade (\u2022\u2022):</b> Whenever a pack member becomes gravely injured or defeated, your character\u2019s Initiative score immediately increases by 2. Additionally, for the duration of the scene your character gains +1 Speed and enemies attempting to affect them with supernatural abilities suffer a -1 penalty to their dice pool; these latter two effects stack, each capped at a value equal to your Primal Urge.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><b>Rivers Of Blood (\u2022\u2022\u2022):</b> Whenever a pack member becomes gravely injured or defeated then your character can transfer a single point of Willpower or Essence from them if the pack member is willing, and gains a single additional health level until the end of the scene; the character can gain up to their Primal Urge in bonus health levels this way. If the injured or fallen were an Uratha pack member and they had yet to enter the Gauru form during the scene, the number of turns your character can spend in Gauru increases by 1 until the end of the scene. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><b>Unstoppable Tide (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022):</b> Whenever an Uratha pack member becomes gravely injured or defeated then your character gains +1 Strength, Dexterity or Wits for the duration of the scene, gaining up to their Primal Urge in bonus attributes in this way.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><b>Infinite Rage (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022): </b>If your character is the last pack member standing after all others have been defeated, then once per scene, if they would be slain by aggravated damage, they can instead remain active for turns equal to the number of defeated pack members, capped at their Primal Urge; during this time they treat aggravated damage as if it were lethal and, if at the end of this period regeneration leaves them on any number of health levels, they will not be slain. If they would be killed by an effect that would slay them without dealing damage, it is instead treated as if it has filled their health boxes with aggravated damage, and they can continue as above while Infinite Rage lasts.</span></div> <div align=\"left\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><b>Drawback: </b>At Harmony 5, your character is still subject to their specific Kuruth trigger, instead of lacking all triggers. After using Infinite Rage, your character is subject to all their Kuruth triggers for a month, instead of whichever ones their Harmony would usually subject them to.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Furious Devotion (\u2022\u2022)</span></b></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><b>Prerequisites:</b> Resolve 3, human or Wolf-Blooded</span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Your character is tied closely to your fellow pack-mates\u2019 anger and determination; their sacrifice gives you strength. For each pack-mate in the scene who has any of their last three health boxes filled with damage due to enemy actions, or who is slain, unconscious, or incapacitated, your character gains +1 Initiative, +1 Speed and +1 to the dice pools on their attacks, up to a maximum equal to their Resolve attribute.</span></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":1757,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","user":"Acrozatarim","date":". 12-30-2017, 01:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-30T11:04:36-08:00","id":1171833,"title":"","content":"I'm loving those Merits - will propose it for our Blood Talon Rahu viking berserker character! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-30T16:38:56-08:00","id":1171918,"title":"","content":"Great use of Styles there. I particularly like how it can be a simple power for the lone combat-oriented member of a standard pack, or can be blown out of proportions and used by some manipulative or charismatic monster in junction with the Great Hunt or Forge Alliance rites as they drive human and wolf-blooded packmates before them, growing more powerful by the death.<br /> <br /> Though I suppose the Primal Urge cap does limit that a pack of werewolves could still take advantage of more replaceable pack members that way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-30T22:04:47-08:00","id":1171956,"title":"","content":"I can see my Ancestor Spirit with Revenge influences handing out this style on totemic benefit. Mad props.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-30T22:17:16-08:00","id":1171957,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1757_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1757\" data-vbnamecard=\"1757\">Acrozatarim</a>, I love the idea - but more I think about it, I have one gripe with <i>Rising Fury </i>- WHY it need Occult Skill as Prerequisites? It's not like they are biding spirits or using truly obscure arcane laws. What does have lore and knowledge about legends to becoming more and more angry as your pack mates fall in the battle? I could understand here high Stamina or maybe Composure - but knowledge of myths?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-30T22:31:05-08:00","id":1171959,"title":"","content":"Because it relies in a transcendence of flesh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-30T22:56:53-08:00","id":1171960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1169612-eleven-shaman-blessings?p=1171959#post1171959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because it relies in a transcendence of flesh.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is <b>nothing</b> related to how Occult work as Skill.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CoD Rulebook, p. 34</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Occult</b><br /> The Occult Skill is a character\u2019s knowledge of myth, folktales, and urban legends about the strange things that exist in the dark corners of the world. Occult can help a character separate fiction and myth from fact and determine which stories are likely to be actual supernatural events and which are just rumors. That said, there are a lot of strange things out there, and many of them defy easy categorization. The Occult Skill doesn\u2019t necessarily give a character a line on the absolute \u201ctruth\u201d about what\u2019s going on, but instead represents an array of knowledge about encounters and theories that others have had, and the ability to build on those theories herself.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-30T23:07:40-08:00","id":1171961,"title":"","content":"P155 'The Occult Skill is your character\u2019s knowledge of things hidden in the dark, legends, and lore. While the supernatural is unpredictable and often unique, the Occult Skill allows your character to pick out facts from rumor. This is a common Skill for werewolves interested in the Shadow; being able to piece together the nature of a spirit from all manner of stories and tales can give insight into the Hisil.'<br /> <br /> The style seems to be something learned from rage and understanding about the pack bond and potentially the regenerative nature of werewolves.<br /> <br /> Allowing you to pick out facts from rumor is an aspect of the Skill, not the sole use of the Skill, similar to how Weaponry can let you identify a fighting style.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-30T23:13:27-08:00","id":1171962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1169612-eleven-shaman-blessings?p=1171960#post1171960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which is <b>nothing</b> related to how Occult work as Skill.</div> </div> </div> </div>A general but firm occult knowledge base doesn't make any sense as the basis for letting you exploit the magical connection between yourself and members of your pack to take unused bits of their strength when they fall in battle, unlike <i>hitting a werewolf so that a bit of their Essence falls out, seeing the last sights of a dead person, moving water around, bringing on a cold snap or a heat wave, </i>or <i>turning your pack totem into an angry werewolf</i>.<br /> <br /> Naturally.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-31T02:17:08-08:00","id":1171978,"title":"","content":"Thanks, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar886_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"886\" data-vbnamecard=\"886\">nofather</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-01T06:11:11-08:00","id":1172235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1169612-eleven-shaman-blessings?p=1170730#post1170730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> (seriously, will we ever get a Lodge/ cult/ potential tribe/ anything more about that elusive Firstborn? Because they are awesome).</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bWho can say? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1169612-eleven-shaman-blessings?p=1171089#post1171089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if there is any promise in a &quot;treat the vessel as the Uratha&quot; Rite. Just general Gift boosts or crazy &quot; my galleon enters Death Rage/Gauru Form&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI think this would depend a lot on how the rules for a vessel actually worked. Most Gift Facets aren't going to have an easy way to be applied to a vehicle, but there are a few that could work for 'upscale this to the entire ship', like Feet of Mist. Most of the rest of the ways to really gel a werewolf to a vessel strike me as working best via treating the crew as pack - probably by just having them literally be inducted into the pack via the normal means, tbh.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-01T06:17:23-08:00","id":1172237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1169612-eleven-shaman-blessings?p=1171250#post1171250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The lunar elementals are really cool, and I may even have the company which distill lunes into them (unless those are Cheiron. Or the Hototogisu. Or Amalgama. Or Daeva. Or Last Dynasties. Or Whiteheart. Yeah, we have a lot of potential candidates for this). I wonder what would happen to regular humans who drink them- the easy answer would be &quot;same as the Pure, more or less&quot;, but I think there are cooler options out there.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI'm roughly inclined to say that they get turned into doppleganger-style shapeshifters; they go mad and their flesh turns into mannequin-like featurelessness, but they gain the ability to perfectly copy other human beings via shapeshifting, and are compelled to do so by the changing phases of the moon.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Oak Prophecy thing is also really great. Loved the God Machine reference- makes me think what leverage does it have to force those ancient, spiteful spirits to its command. I also feel like I should know why oaks can lie in their prophesies, but I can't put the finger on it- which is a good thing. Loved that they are presented in a way which is so drastically different from the cultural representations of oaks- that is, of old, smart and generous trees. I wonder if other tree spirits would have similar quirks, which sounds kinda cool, IMO. </div> </div> </div>\u200bMy preference runs for there being lots of local/regional/subspecies-style unique quirks and traits. Makes it so that knowing the Shadow's irregularities has meaning, and so that going to a new area means you have to try and tap into the existing Uratha knowledge base of how to deal with stuff even if you're a veteran Shadow explorer.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-01T08:06:04-08:00","id":1172261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1169612-eleven-shaman-blessings?p=1172235#post1172235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bI think this would depend a lot on how the rules for a vessel actually worked. Most Gift Facets aren't going to have an easy way to be applied to a vehicle, but there are a few that could work for 'upscale this to the entire ship', like Feet of Mist. Most of the rest of the ways to really gel a werewolf to a vessel strike me as working best via treating the crew as pack - probably by just having them literally be inducted into the pack via the normal means, tbh.</div> </div> </div> </div>True. Maybe a Fetish (Figurehead?) that specifically expands only certain Facets over the entire ship, then?<br /> <br /> Though the mental image of a ship repairing all damage in moments, continuously, to their opponent's horror (Ship in Death Rage) is amusing.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}